FIFA 19 is nearly here in case you  hadn't heard it adds the Champions  League license to the FIFA franchise for  the first time in a decade unlucky the  PES but some fans have criticized EA for  changing little else about this year's  game than some small tweaks to Ultimate  Team at Gamescom I spoke to Sam Rivera  FIFA's leaked gameplay producer who  confirmed to us that pro clubs has no  new editions except for some new  licenses while career mode has basically  nothing new except some paltry new  additions like the addition of a star  above your club bad if you win the  Champions League but once you get onto  the pitch FIFA 19 is packed full of  small but meaningful tweaks so here are  19 new features that we thought were  worth your attention straight off the  bat EA have attempted to add a little  bit more depth to FIFA shooting this  year with the addition of timed  finishing you can now attempt to hit a  shot even sweeter than before by tapping  circle or B a second time just as your  foot hits the ball get the timing right  and there's a decent chance the ball be  flying into the top corner follow my  example and it will probably end up in  rosette or end up squashing a few days  he's around the corner flag  if you're the sort of FIFA player who  likes to play it from the back then this  one's for you you know when you're  playing next to a friend and you want to  play it to your centre back all right  back from a goal kick but if you move  the stick  you'll make you'll see the camera swing  around and know where you're gonna pass  to now moving the stick from a goal kick  doesn't move the camera so you can  emulate Barcelona and Manchester City T  heart's content  one of the pair's 2018 s best small  improvements was a gray marker above the  currently selected second player when  defending this allows you to know which  second man will press and which player  you'll switch to should you press l1 or  left bumper EA has smartly borrowed the  idea and put it into FIFA 19  [Music]  passing in general feels better this  year but the biggest step forward has  been seen in through passes which feel  much more natural they feel way more  powerful too powerful in fact and I  wouldn't be surprised to see them nerfed  before launch I mean just look at the  stay of these filthy passes  [Applause]  Jordan headed Marnie ei says that 50/50  battles over a loose ball may take into  account many more variables than they  did last year in our playtime these  battles for the possession didn't appear  to have the frustrating unpredictability  of FIFA's past instead 50 50 battles  felt more responsive taking into account  player attributes and user reaction  times for all the wannabe football  managers out there EA has greatly  expanded FIFA's tactical options this  year for example you can now tell your  full bets what kind of runs to make when  on the attack on top of that you can  also tell a central midfielder to cover  the wing or the center of the park quite  why you'd ever want them standing on the  touchline when the ball is in the middle  is beyond me  full disclosure I am colorblind which in  the past has made it quite difficult to  tell which team is which on FIFA's  mini-map thankfully in FIFA 19 1 0 half  triangular icons as opposed to the  standard circular ones  [Applause]  off the pitch game plans are a new  feature that allow you to configure  alternate tactical options before the  match this means you can now have  separate game plans for when you one  kneel down and need to go on the  offensive  pushing for backs up and having more  players throughout the box obviously and  for when you tune it up and want to  protect your lead unfortunately this  means the old presets all-out attack and  part the busts are a thing of the past  staying within the menus you can also  now have greater control over your  team's defensive style that means you  can change the way your team attempt to  reclaim the ball via the following  settings pressure after possession loss  constant pressure drop back balanced and  pressure on heavy touch  and ass has become a common feature in  football games you can now adjust your  team's width and depth in FIFA 19  however you can also adjust the number  of players you send forward for corner  kicks and tweak how many players will  make forward runs in play the champion Z  will of course be seen in the journey  ultimate team and career mode but will  also get its own standalone mode within  that you can set up a custom Champions  League and have it include any team you  like or you can also play a Champions  League branded match with any two teams  in kickoff great news for all the  Arsenal fans out there  and this next point probably got a  little lost in the excitement of getting  the Champions League license but the  Europa League would also be in FIFA 19  great news for all the Arsenal fans out  there  back on the pitch headers now feel far  more satisfying whether it should play a  hanging in the air that little bit  longer when jumping or timing their run  to perfection headers have a dynamism to  them that make them feel much more  powerful than before  [Applause]  in fact player animation across the  board feels way smoother thanks in part  to the active touch system the new  system allows for better first touches  with many different parts of the body  which both looks great and gives you  greater control over the ball chief  among these new animations is a new  faint move which means you can now faint  to go in one direction before touching  the ball off in the opposite direction  and then there's the updated animations  for step overs which appear to be easier  to trigger and a little more powerful  than before one of the most annoying  things about previous FIFA games is that  it was never totally clear whether  in-game tactical options such as forcing  your defense to play an offside trap  were activated once you click the button  you never knew whether it would be  active permanently or if it was just  temporary and whether or not it was  currently active this year there's a  clear toggle so you know when you're  telling a centre-back to join the attack  I mean you should probably be able to  tell from the 6 foot 6 inch lump there  standing on the goal line so if not you  should probably get your eyes checked  a neat little addition within the match  preview screen is the detailed stats  menu effectively an extended score sheet  these exhaustive menus will keep track  of all your play session stats against  your opponent whether it's AI or your  mate sitting next to you maybe you'd  like to play best of five whereas your  mate likes to settle the winner on  aggregate regardless it will be within  these menus that those petty arguments  will be settled look I told you decided  my aggregate is for Champions League  matches will feature these funky looking  banners in the build-up to each match  now I know that's a tiny detail but I am  a sucker for neat little touches like  that  [Music]  last and probably fair to say least is  the clock in stoppage time as the game  enters into its final moments the clock  no longer freezes at ninety minutes  instead continuing on to show you how  much injury time you have left it's not  exactly a grain breaking edition but  it's appreciated all the same  there are 19 new additions and  enhancements that we saw in our time  with FIFA 19 let us know your thoughts  on FIFA 19 good and bad in the comments  section below or you can come and  complain to me on twitter i'm at dare  said and i'll see you next time  you
 

